From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: build the recovered ISP driver on Linux 7.x

Port the recovered T41 driver and its V4L2 frontend from the vendor 4.4
API to the mainline 7.x API:

- add a T41 kernel-compat header (timeval, wait_queue_t, strlcpy,
  PDE_DATA, set_fs/KERNEL_DS, do_gettimeofday, monotonic clock, div64)
- add a compat object for the Ingenic SDK/proc/cache/DMA helpers
- use copy_from_kernel_nofault, i2c_new_client_device, kernel_read/write,
  kmalloc, timer_setup/timer_delete_sync, ioremap/iounmap
- adapt the V4L2 frontend to the 7.x videobuf2 API and VFL_TYPE_VIDEO

Build-tested for compile and link only; it has not been loaded or probed
on hardware yet.
---
